    "questions": [
      {
        "dom_id": "question-334767",
        "name": "Question 1",
        "problem": "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-5x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-5y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-5t} & t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.$*",
        "answer_fields_complete": true,
        "result": "Correct",
