        "solution_binding": "a76bd3d73bcc1d3723832c7306d5e0790127978bc91f988b34f2eccc6fb99617",
        "accepted": true,
        "feedback": {
          "dom_id": "question-334769",
          "name": null,
          "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=8y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8t} & t{e}^{8t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{8t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].$*",
          "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8t} & t{e}^{8t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{8t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8t} & t{e}^{8t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{8t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{8t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{8t} \\\\ {e}^{8t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$",
