        "solution": {
          "status": "ambiguous",
          "reasoning": "The solution is e^{A(t+2)}(0,−2)ᵀ, giving x(t)=−2sinh(2(t+2)) and y(t)=−2cosh(2(t+2)), exactly option d. At t=−2 these equal 0 and −2; differentiation verifies x'=2y and y'=2x. No captured Math Academy answer or grade establishes its key.",
          "confidence": 1,
          "answers": [
            {
              "key": "selection",
              "correct_value": "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{aligned}]",
              "correct_option": "d",
              "value_type": "math",
              "wrong_value": null,
              "correct_keys": [],
              "wrong_keys": [],
              "ma_value": null,
              "ma_basis": "none",
